  "number": 6028,
  "title": "Convert the default and initials avatars to CSS modules",
  "body": "> Continues the CSS Modules migration (#5997, #6024) with the avatars.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Changed\n\n- Converted the default and initials avatars to CSS Modules with `webchat__` class names; `avatarBorderRadius`, `botAvatarBackgroundColor` and `userAvatarBackgroundColor` are now custom properties, in PR [#6028](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6028), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n### Removed\n\n- 💥 Deprecated the `avatar` and `initialsAvatar` style set entries, which no longer affect rendering, in PR [#6028](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6028), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nThe default and initials avatars move from emotion style sets to CSS Modules. No snapshot changes; rendered class names stay.\n\n## Design\n\n- `avatarBorderRadius` sets the reserved `--webchat__border-radius--avatar`; backgrounds use `--webchat__background--avatar(-user)` with the `accent` fallback in JavaScript (a CSS `var()` fallback would give Fluent avatars Fluent's accent).\n- One `Avatar.module.css` with 3 regions takes over `ImageAvatar.module.css`.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `DefaultAvatar`, `InitialsAvatar`, `ImageAvatar`: `Avatar/Avatar.module.css`, `InferReactProps`\n- `CustomPropertyNames.ts`, `CSSCustomPropertiesContainer.tsx`: 3 avatar custom properties\n- `createStyleSet.ts`, `StyleSet/{Avatar,InitialsAvatar}.ts`: `@deprecated`\n- `fluentCSSModuleTheme.module.css`: `stacked-loyout__bubble` typo → `stacked-layout__bubble`, no visible change\n- `styleOptions/avatarBorderRadius.html`: new page, numeric radius (4 px corners)\n- `DefaultAvatar.spec.tsx` CSS mock; `imageAvatar` JSDoc paths\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n\n",
